new file mode 100644
index 0000000..59ed1c8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# Chat Bots Architecture
+
+## Data Model
+- Bots are stored as `User` records with `role: :bot` (enum values: `member: 0, administrator: 1, bot: 2`).
+- `users.bot_token` stores a 24-character `SecureRandom.base58` credential (unique indexed, filtered from logs and `inspect` via `:token` in `filter_parameters`).
+- `users.creator_id` references the `User` who created the bot, enabling `User#can_administer?(bot)` for creators and administrators.
+- `users.add_to_all_open_rooms` (boolean, default `false`) controls whether a bot automatically joins open rooms. Unlike human users, bots no longer join `Rooms::Open` by default.
+- When `add_to_all_open_rooms` is enabled on create or update, `User::Bot#sync_open_room_memberships` grants membership to all existing `Rooms::Open` (skipping rooms the bot already belongs to). `Rooms::Open#grant_access_to_all_users` grants access to `User.open_room_members` (`User.active.without_bots` plus `User.bots.where(add_to_all_open_rooms: true)`). Disabling `add_to_all_open_rooms` preserves existing memberships.
+- Deleting a bot calls `User#deactivate`, which sets `status: :deactivated`, clears `bot_token: nil`, `webhook_url: nil`, `add_to_all_open_rooms: false`, and removes non-direct memberships while preserving previously posted messages.
+- Human-only flows (`SessionsController`, `Sessions::TransfersController`, `AccountsController`, `Accounts::UsersController`, `Users::SidebarsController`) scope with `User.without_bots`.
+
+## UI Routes & Access Control
+- `/account/edit` exposes the "Set up chat bots" link (`/bots`) to all signed-in members.
+- `BotsController` (`/bots`, `/bots/new`, `/bots/:id/edit`) lists `Current.user.created_bots.active` for members and all `User.bots` for administrators on a single unpaginated page.
+- Bot forms (`app/views/bots/_form.html.erb`) expose `"Name the bot"`, optional `"Webhook URL"`, and the `"Add to all open rooms"` checkbox switch (off by default).
+- `edit`, `update`, and `destroy` require `Current.user.can_administer?(@bot)` (creator or administrator).
+- `Account#settings` includes `bots_per_member` (integer, default `5`, validated `>= 0`), configurable by administrators on `/account/edit` under `"Bots per member"`.
+- `User::Bot#bot_limit_reached?` counts `created_bots.active` (deactivated/deleted bots do not count) against `Account#settings.bots_per_member`; administrators are exempt.
+- At or above the limit, `/bots` hides `"Add a chat bot"` and states the member has `"reached the limit"`. `BotsController#new` and `#create` return `403 Forbidden`, and `User::Bot` validates the limit `on: :create` so lowering the limit blocks new bots without removing or blocking edits/deletions of existing bots.
+
+## HTTP Message API
+- `POST /rooms/:room_id/:bot_token/messages` (`Bots::MessagesController#create`) authenticates via `User.find_by_bot_token` and scopes the room to `@bot.rooms`.
+- For non-multipart requests, `Bots::MessagesController#process_action` sets `request.request_parameters = {}` before `super` so Rails/Rack never attempts to form-parse or JSON-parse raw text bodies (e.g. `curl -d "100% done"`).
+- Raw bodies are UTF-8 normalized, HTML-escaped, and newline-converted before saving as ActionText `Message` bodies; `multipart/form-data` requests with `attachment` use `create_with_attachment!`.
+- Responses: `201 Created` (`Location: /messages/:message_id`), `422 Unprocessable Content`, `404 Not Found`, `401 Unauthorized`.
+
+## Outgoing Webhooks & Synchronous/Async Replies
+- `users.webhook_url` (optional string) is normalized (`strip.presence`), validated as an `http`/`https` URL when present, and cleared alongside `bot_token` on `User#deactivate`.
+- `Message::Mentionee#mentioned_bots` selects active bots that are members of the room (excluding `message.creator`) referenced in ActionText mention attachments.
+- `Room#receive(message)` enqueues `User::Bot::WebhookJob` (`event: "mention"`) per mentioned bot with a `webhook_url`.
+- Whenever a bot with a `webhook_url` is newly added to a non-direct room (`Rooms::Open` or `Rooms::Closed`)—whether via `Room#memberships.grant_to`, `Membership.create!`, `Rooms::Open` creation/conversion, or `add_to_all_open_rooms`—`Room#deliver_joined_webhooks_later` / `User::Bot#deliver_joined_webhook_later` enqueues `User::Bot::WebhookJob` (`event: "joined"`) once per newly added `(bot, room)` pair. `Rooms::Direct` never triggers `joined`.
+- `User::Bot::WebhookJob` uses `enqueue_after_transaction_commit = true` so workers only run after memberships and rooms are committed.
+- `User::Bot::Webhook` POSTs `Content-Type: application/json` for `mention` (`event`, `author`, `room`, `message`) and `joined` (`event: "joined"`, `room: { id, name, reply_to }`).
+- Synchronous `200` responses with `Content-Type: text/plain` (HTML-escaped with `<br>` newlines) or `text/html` create and broadcast a reply message from the bot; `204` or non-matching responses post nothing.
+
+## Bot Moderation (Flooding, Failing Webhooks, Suspension & Reactivation)
+- Moderation state lives on `users` (`suspended_at`, `suspension_reason`, `cooldown_until`, `cooldown_attempts`, `consecutive_webhook_failures`, `flood_reset_message_id`), keeping `status: :active` so suspended bots retain rooms/messages, still count toward `bot_limit_reached?`, stay listed on `/bots`, and remain editable/deletable by creators and admins.
+- `User::Bot#post_message_with_rate_limit` wraps message creation in `with_lock` (SQLite immediate transaction) so API posts (`Bots::MessagesController#create`) and synchronous webhook replies (`User::Bot::Webhook#handle_response`) share one atomic 10-messages-in-10-seconds sliding window (`messages` indexed on `[:creator_id, :created_at]`).
+- Exceeding 10 messages in 10 seconds rejects the message and starts a 30-second cooldown (`429 Too Many Requests` + `Retry-After` seconds left; webhook replies are not posted). Five more post attempts during the same cooldown suspend the bot (`FLOODING_SUSPENSION_REASON`).
+- `User::Bot#record_webhook_delivery!` tracks `consecutive_webhook_failures`: any non-`2xx` response, timeout, or connection error increments the counter (suspending at 10 with `WEBHOOK_SUSPENSION_REASON`), while any `2xx` response resets it to `0`.
+- Suspended bots receive `403 Forbidden` from `Bots::MessagesController` (`ensure_not_suspended` before `set_room`) and receive no webhooks (`Message::Mentionee#mentioned_bots`, `Room#deliver_joined_webhooks_later`, `User::Bot#deliver_*_webhook_later`, and `User::Bot::Webhook#deliverable?` all skip suspended bots).
+- `/bots` (`app/views/bots/_bot.html.erb`) displays `"Suspended"` and `bot.suspension_reason` to both owners and administrators, and renders a `"Reactivate"` button (`POST /bots/:bot_id/reactivation`, `Bots::ReactivationsController#create` guarded by `ensure_can_administer`) with `data-turbo-confirm` solely for administrators.
+- `User::Bot#reactivate` clears suspension/cooldown/webhook failure counters and records `flood_reset_message_id` so the reactivated bot can post immediately without pre-suspension messages counting against the 10-second window.
